BT /F1 9 Tf 40 750 Td 14 TL (STATEMENT OF WITNESS UNDER SECTION 161 Cr.P.C. / SECTION 180 BNSS, 2023) ' (POLICE STATION: EOW, Mandir Marg, New Delhi | FIR NO: 0412/2024) ' (DATE OF EXAMINATION: 18/08/2024 | INVESTIGATING OFFICER: SI Devendra Chawla) ' (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) ' (WITNESS IDENTIFICATION:) ' (Name: Ramesh Gupta, S/o Late K. L. Gupta, Age: 44 Years) ' (Designation: Chief Financial Officer, Apex FinTech Innovations Ltd., Gurugram.) ' (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) ' (WITNESS TESTIMONY:) ' (I am the Chief Financial Officer of Apex FinTech Innovations Ltd. since January 2021.) ' (I was personally involved in negotiating the financial terms of the Master Agreement dated 15/01/2024.) ' (On 04/02/2024, Accused No. 2 Sameer Verma emailed the CertiGuard escrow receipt to my corporate email address.) ' (I verified the email attachment and authorized the RTGS payment of INR 4,25,00,000/- on 05/02/2024.) ' () ' (CONCERNING THE INCIDENT OF 10/08/2024 \(CROSS-EXAMINATION / CONTRADICTION POINT\):) ' (On 10/08/2024, at approximately 11:30 AM, I accompanied MD Vikramaditya Singhania to Zenith's Okhla office.) ' (Accused Rajesh Malhotra was present in the boardroom along with two private security guards.) ' (When our MD demanded immediate access to the GitHub enterprise escrow keys, Rajesh Malhotra shouted at us.) ' (However, contrary to what was later stated in the FIR, there was NO physical violence or assault whatsoever.) ' (Rajesh Malhotra merely slammed the desk, hurled verbal abuses, and asked us to resolve the dispute in arbitration.) ' (Neither I nor Mr. Singhania suffered any bodily blows, fractures, or physical injury during this entire meeting.) ' (We left the Okhla premises peacefully at 12:15 PM and drove back to our Gurugram corporate headquarters.) ' () ' (CONCERNING PRE-DISBURSEMENT DUE DILIGENCE & SOFTWARE INTEGRATION:) ' (I state that our technical team led by Mr. Singhania had already inspected the beta software build in January 2024.) ' (The software architecture was working properly in the staging environment before any funds were released.) ' (The dispute arose primarily because Zenith demanded an additional INR 1.5 Crores for cloud GPU server costs.) ' (Statement recorded verbatim without fear, favor, or coercion.) ' (Sd/- Ramesh Gupta \(Witness / CFO\).) ' ET
